# Front-end style

Full rationale lives in `STYLE_GUIDE.md` — read it once, then follow these
rules on every change:

- Use `shadcn/ui` primitives from `src/components/ui/` for every button,
  input, dialog, badge, tooltip, card, etc. Never hand-roll one. Missing a
  primitive? Run `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component>`.
- Only use the color tokens defined in `src/app/globals.css`
  (`bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-primary`, ...). Don't
  inline new hex/oklch colors.
- Icons: `lucide-react` for UI chrome, `react-icons/gi` only through the
  curated map in `src/lib/icons.ts` for the campaign map.
- Any user-facing image must go through
  `src/components/editable-image.tsx` so hover-to-replace works
  consistently.
- Default to Server Components; add `"use client"` only to the specific
  interactive island that needs state/effects/browser APIs.
- Every list/empty state renders a short, friendly message — never a blank
  screen.
- Keep filenames kebab-case, components PascalCase, one component per
  file.
